        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(config): ignore inherited keys when restoring env refs",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nUse `Object.hasOwn(parsed, key)` when restoring environment references so inherited properties are not treated as authored configuration.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\n`restoreEnvVarRefs` accepts plain-object values whose prototype may be customized. Its object branch iterates own `incoming` entries, but the previous `key in parsed` check also admitted inherited `parsed` properties. An inherited environment-reference template could therefore replace an incoming own value even though that template was never authored on the parsed object.\n\n## Root Cause\n\n- `in` traverses the prototype chain.\n- `Object.hasOwn` matches the authored-key semantics used by adjacent config helpers.\n- `isPlainObject` intentionally accepts custom prototypes, so narrowing the membership check is the correct local owner-boundary fix.\n\n## Why This Fix\n\n- One canonical own-property check at the restoration decision.\n- No parser normalization, compatibility shim, or broader `isPlainObject` contract change.\n- Matches sibling config-path and merge-patch own-key handling.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNormal JSON and JSON5 config behavior is unchanged. Internal or custom callers that pass plain objects with custom prototypes no longer restore inherited environment-reference templates.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- The original submitted test also passed with the old implementation, so the maintainer fixup replaced it.\n- The repaired regression creates a custom prototype carrying an inherited template.\n- With `key in parsed`, the focused suite fails because the inherited template is restored.\n- With `Object.hasOwn`, the incoming value is preserved.\n\n## Tests and Validation\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox baseline: 1 focused regression failure with the old membership check.\n- Blacksmith Testbox fixed: `src/config/env-preserve.test.ts` passed, 72/72 tests.\n- Targeted `oxfmt --check` passed.\n- Maintainer autoreview passed with no findings.\n- Exact-head hosted CI is required before merge.\n\n## Changelog\n\nNot required: internal hardening with no documented JSON or JSON5 behavior change.\n",
